    "grammar": [
      {
        "title": "Adjective before the noun",
        "explanation_ar": "في العربية تأتي الصفة بعد الموصوف (مشكلة كبيرة)، أما في الإنجليزية فتأتي الصفة قبل الاسم: a big problem. ولا نجمع الصفة أبداً: two major problems وليس majors.",
        "explanation_en": "In Arabic the adjective comes after the noun. In English it comes before the noun: a big problem. Adjectives have no plural: two major problems.",
        "examples": [
          "two major problems",
          "a special suit",
          "a red car"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Adjective after be",
        "explanation_ar": "تأتي الصفة أيضاً بعد فعل be لتصف الفاعل: The test is easy. Your answer is right.",
        "explanation_en": "An adjective can also come after the verb \"be\" to describe the subject: The test is easy.",
        "examples": [
          "The weather is bad.",
          "The market is open now.",
          "This bag is light."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Comparatives: -er and more",
        "explanation_ar": "للمقارنة نضيف er للصفات القصيرة (large → larger, small → smaller)، ونستخدم more مع الصفات الطويلة (more important). وهناك شواذ: good → better، bad → worse.",
        "explanation_en": "To compare, add -er to short adjectives (larger) and use \"more\" with long ones (more important). Irregular: good → better, bad → worse.",
        "examples": [
          "We need a larger car.",
          "Health is more important than money.",
          "Today is better than yesterday."
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "a or an depends on the adjective",
        "explanation_ar": "نختار a أو an حسب أول صوت في الكلمة التي تليها مباشرة، وقد تكون صفة: a joke لكن an old joke؛ an apple لكن a new apple.",
        "explanation_en": "Choose a or an by the first sound of the next word, which may be an adjective: a joke, but an old joke.",
        "examples": [
          "an old joke",
          "a new idea",
          "an easy question"
        ]
      },
      {
        "title": "Adjective vs adverb",
        "explanation_ar": "الصفة تصف الاسم (a good student)، والظرف يصف الفعل (study well). كثير من الظروف نصنعها بإضافة ly للصفة: quick → quickly. لكن good تصبح well.",
        "explanation_en": "An adjective describes a noun; an adverb describes a verb. Many adverbs add -ly: quick → quickly. But good → well.",
        "examples": [
          "She is a good driver.",
          "She drives well.",
          "He speaks quickly."
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
